harpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block:conclusion:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block:0"],"kind":"dock","label":"SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block","nodeId":"c:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw","semanticId":"Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block"},"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform:assumption:Lax342547.FiniteLinearLaw:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform:conclusion:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Prescribe the chosen forward block and set its reverse to zero. Disjoint\nindex sets make these prescriptions consistent, so the alternating-block\nobservation is a surjective linear map and hence has the uniform law.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform","tooltipHtml":"Prescribe the chosen forward block and set its reverse to zero. Disjoint\nindex sets make these prescriptions consistent, so the alternating-block\nobservation is a surjective linear map and hence has the uniform law."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound:assumption:Lax342547.LowRankCounting:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound:assumption:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_block_uniform:0","e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound:conclusion:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.alternating_low_rank_bound:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"Use the disjoint even and odd indices for a square block of side floor(n/2).\nIts rank cannot exceed the rank of the alternating matrix, and its uniform\nlaw satisfies the rectangular low-rank probability bound.","node