bel":"Distinct labels differ in some bit, so their coefficient sum at that bit\nis nonzero in the binary field. The weighted matrix map is surjective.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.label_weighted_uniform","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.label_weighted_uniform","tooltipHtml":"Distinct labels differ in some bit, so their coefficient sum at that bit\nis nonzero in the binary field. The weighted matrix map is surjective."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block:conclusion:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"All tester and sharp coordinates vanish on a free Z-direction input.\nConsequently an optional self-Gram evaluation contributes zero to the\nfree-direction block used to test a nonempty mixer parity.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_free_block","tooltipHtml":"All tester and sharp coordinates vanish on a free Z-direction input.\nConsequently an optional self-Gram evaluation contributes zero to the\nfree-direction block used to test a nonempty mixer parity."},"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block":{"href":"../lax-342547/Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block.html","incident":["e:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block:conclusion:Lax342547.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block:0"],"kind":"proof","label":"The ordinary and shared testers vanish on sharp directions. Evaluating\nthe remaining form gives the selector sum s_a+t_a multiplying M_a.\nApply the bilinear form to basis vectors to recover the whole matrix block.","nodeId":"p:Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block","semanticId":"Lax342547Proofs.SharpMixerLaw.selfGram_sharp_block","tooltipHtml":"The ordinary and shared testers vanish on sharp directions. Evaluating\nthe re